<div class="mt-8 space-y-8">
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Purpose and scope</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">The Provider will make the DigitoFina financial management platform available to the Customer for the license or service period stated above. The platform may include organization management, branches, users, clients, savings, loans, accounting, reporting, integrations, and other enabled modules.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Platform operation and data flow</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">The Customer accesses the platform through supported web or mobile interfaces using authorized accounts. Customer users enter or import operational information such as client profiles, applications, approvals, repayments, savings, accounting entries, reports, and audit events. The platform validates and stores that information in the Customer’s organization space, applies role and branch permissions, and makes the resulting records available to authorized users and reports.</p><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Information may move between enabled platform modules so that, for example, a loan workflow can update schedules and balances, a payment can update the relevant account and ledger records, and reports can summarize authorized transactions. Integrations, notifications, backups, hosting providers, and other service components may process data only as needed to provide, secure, maintain, or support the agreed service.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Access controls and audit records</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Each party will use named accounts where available and limit access according to job responsibilities. Organization, branch, role, and administrator permissions determine which records a user may view or change. The platform may record sign-ins, changes, approvals, exports, reversals, and other security or operational events for audit, troubleshooting, fraud prevention, and compliance purposes.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Hosting, backups, and data recovery</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">The Provider will host the service using reasonable operational safeguards and maintain routine backups according to the service’s operating procedures. Backups support recovery and continuity but do not replace the Customer’s responsibility to verify important records, maintain lawful retention practices, and promptly report suspected loss, unauthorized access, or inaccurate data.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Provider responsibilities</h2><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-700"><li>Provide access to the agreed DigitoFina modules and maintain the production service with reasonable care.</li><li>Apply security updates, maintain routine backups, and use reasonable measures to protect Customer data.</li><li>Respond to reported faults within a reasonable time and communicate material service incidents where practical.</li><li>Provide ordinary user guidance and reasonable product updates during the term.</li><li>Discuss requested customizations in good faith and confirm separate scope, price, and delivery dates before chargeable work begins.</li><li>Keep Customer information confidential, subject to lawful disclosure.</li></ul></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Customer responsibilities</h2><ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-700"><li>Pay all agreed fees and provide accurate organization, branch, user, client, and contact information.</li><li>Use the platform lawfully and only for authorized operations.</li><li>Keep passwords, devices, API credentials, and administrator access secure.</li><li>Ensure that Customer data is accurate and that users have appropriate permissions.</li><li>Provide timely decisions, test data, approvals, and access needed for agreed configuration or customization work.</li><li>Maintain its own internet connectivity, devices, local policies, and third-party services.</li></ul></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Data ownership and confidentiality</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">The Customer retains ownership of data submitted to the platform. The Provider may process that data to operate, secure, support, improve, and lawfully administer the service. Each party will protect the other party’s confidential information using reasonable safeguards.</p><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">The Provider may use aggregated and de-identified operational statistics for service monitoring and improvement, provided those statistics do not identify the Customer, its clients, or individual transactions.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Support, updates, and customization</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Routine updates, bug fixes, security improvements, and ordinary configuration are included unless the commercial terms state otherwise. Custom features, data migration, special reports, integrations, additional training, and onsite work may be quoted separately.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Availability and service limits</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">The Provider will use reasonable efforts to keep the service available. Planned maintenance, emergency maintenance, internet failures, third-party outages, force majeure events, and Customer-controlled systems may affect availability. The platform does not replace the Customer’s legal, accounting, credit, data protection, or internal control responsibilities.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Term, renewal, and review</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">{{ $contract->term_type === 'perpetual' ? 'This is a one-time perpetual license. Annual hosting and any separately agreed services remain payable.' : 'This agreement continues for '.$contract->term_months.' months from the agreed effective date.' }} The parties may renew or revise the commercial terms in writing. Pricing may be reviewed with reference to branches, users, clients, enabled modules, transaction volume, storage, integrations, and support or customization requirements.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Suspension and termination</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Either party may terminate for a material breach that remains uncured 30 days after written notice. The Provider may suspend access where necessary to protect the platform, comply with law, address a security threat, or respond to serious misuse. On termination, outstanding amounts remain payable and a reasonable Customer data export may be made available.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Liability</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">Each party remains responsible for its own acts and omissions. To the extent permitted by law, neither party is liable for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential loss. The Provider’s total liability arising from this agreement will not exceed the fees paid or payable by the Customer during the 12 months before the event giving rise to the claim, except where liability cannot lawfully be limited.</p></section>
    <section><h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Governing law and notices</h2><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">This agreement is governed by the laws of Uganda. The parties will first try to resolve disputes through good-faith senior management discussions. Formal notices may be sent to the agreed addresses and email contacts.</p></section>
</div>
